---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import shotBanner from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-expand-run-banner-shot.webp';
import detailHover from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-hover.webp';
import detailConsent from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-consent.webp';
import detailBanner from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-banner.webp';
import detailBound from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-bound.webp';
import detailLookups from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-lookups.webp';
import detailSaved from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-expand-saved.webp';
---
<!-- Chapter 1b: Expand with Sources (0131). Written 2026-08-20 from
     flow-expand-with-sources-source.md. Every number below is a recorded
     figure from that shoot's two billed runs on the development build; the
     operator accepted dev-build shots as launch-ready on 2026-08-20.
     TRUTH RAILS (the brief's hard guardrails, each one load-bearing):
       * hosted Anthropic models only today; NEVER say a lookup runs locally
         or costs $0.00 (the owned-runtime carrier is goal 0142, unbuilt);
       * no citations, no snapshots, no source-scope picker (goal 0074);
       * no fetch demo: the public-page fetch scope is closed today;
       * the estimate (0.000924 USD, from the price table) and the recorded
         cost (0.026684 USD, after the run) are TWO facts, never one;
       * the 12-lookup bound is a feature, not an apology;
       * do not oversell retrieval: name what each lookup retrieved, even
         when it was the document itself.
     No of-stage here on purpose: the page's stage corners (toolbar --tl,
     long documents --br) stay adjacent and tests/e2e/product-stage asserts
     adjacency in rendered order. -->
<section class="border-t border-border/60 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-expand">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Expand with Sources</p>
      <h3 id="tour-expand" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">The AI agent that shows you its work before it acts.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">
        Expand with Sources lets a model use Flow's own lookups: read the document and search
        the folders you have open. Every lookup is shown live while it runs, the run is bounded
        and you can stop it, and the final write arrives as the same approved diff as every
        other run. Other agents run their tools out of sight and hand you a result to trust.
        Flow runs them behind the machinery it already owns: scope, consent, live narration,
        approval, and a receipt.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted" data-animate="rise">
        Today a run with lookups is carried by hosted Anthropic models only, and fetching public
        pages stays switched off. Both are stated on screen before you click.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="flow-path mt-12" data-animate-stagger="slow">
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">Before the click</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">The whole bargain, stated first.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">
            Hover the Ex monogram and the panel says what would run: 99 words of selection,
            under a cent estimated from Flow's price table, Claude Haiku 4.5, that the text
            leaves this Mac, and the routing rule that decided it. Nothing has run yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail
          src={detailHover}
          class="w-full max-w-[34rem]"
          alt="Flow's tool strip with the Expand with Sources panel open: 99 words, selection; under $0.01 estimated from Flow price table v2; Claude Haiku 4.5, Leaves this Mac, decided by the rule 'Can hold the whole document'."
          caption="Scope, cost, model, locality, and the deciding rule · All before anything runs"
          sizes="(min-width: 900px) 34rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        />
      </li>
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">Consent</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">Itemized, and bounded to reading.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">
            The sheet names the destination, lists the sources it will send by filename with
            a size (two items, about one kilobyte), and states the estimate to the digit:
            0.000924 USD, priced from the table before the run. One sentence bounds the
            authority: read access only. Editing, browsing, publishing, messaging, and
            spending each need their own permission.
          </p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail
          src={detailConsent}
          class="w-full max-w-[43rem]"
          alt="Flow's consent sheet titled 'Leaves this Mac': destination Anthropic, one included source with '2 items, approximately 1 KB', 'Estimated 0.000924 USD', the read-access-only sentence, and Cancel and Allow Once buttons."
          caption="Destination, sources, estimate to the digit · Read access only"
          sizes="(min-width: 900px) 34rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        />
      </li>
    </ol>

    <!-- Mid-flight: the whole window, because the banner and the title-bar
         readout are the two places the run shows itself, and they sit at
         opposite ends of the frame. 2560x1440 capture, so natural aspect. -->
    <div class="mt-14">
      <FlowShot
        src={shotBanner}
        alt="Orionfold Flow mid-run: the banner reads 'Expanding with sources' and lists three folder searches already made, the title bar counts tokens and dollars as they accrue, and the Receipts pane sits beside the document."
        caption="Mid-flight · Each lookup narrated as it happens, pause and stop one click away"
        natural
        sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="bench-honesty mx-auto mt-14" data-animate-stagger="slow">
      <div class="bench-honesty__item" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="bench-honesty__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">During the run</p>
          <h4 class="bench-honesty__head">It narrates every lookup, live.</h4>
          <p class="bench-honesty__body">
            The banner streams each lookup as it happens and names the carrier. The title bar
            counts real tokens and dollars as they accrue. Pause and stop stay one click away
            for the whole run.
          </p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail
          src={detailBanner}
          alt="Flow's run banner: 'Expanding with sources...' with three lines, each 'Searched your folders for' a quoted phrase, the carrier 'Anthropic · claude-haiku-4-5' at the right, and pause and stop controls."
          caption="Searched your folders for … · Anthropic, claude-haiku-4-5 · Pause, stop"
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 62rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="bench-honesty__item" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="bench-honesty__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">The bound</p>
          <h4 class="bench-honesty__head">A run that hits its limit ends itself, and says so.</h4>
          <p class="bench-honesty__body">
            Every run is bounded: 12 lookups and 180 seconds. This one spent its lookups
            and stopped. The banner says it plainly: the run reached its limit of 12 lookups,
            and nothing in the document was changed. No partial write, no silent retry. That
            is the product refusing to run away with your money.
          </p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail
          src={detailBound}
          alt="Flow's run banner after a bounded run: 'The run ended early. The run reached its limit of 12 lookups. Nothing in the document was changed. Try running Expand with Sources again.'"
          caption="The run reached its limit of 12 lookups · Nothing in the document was changed"
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 62rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <ol class="flow-path mt-14" data-animate-stagger="slow">
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">After approval</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">Every lookup, in order, in the receipt.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">
            The run card leads the document's Receipts pane. One read of the document, then
            nine folder searches, each with its query, what it retrieved, and how long it
            took. Named honestly: most of these searches came back with the document being
            expanded, and the receipt says exactly that rather than claiming research it did
            not do.
          </p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail
          src={detailLookups}
          class="w-full max-w-[37.5rem]"
          alt="The Lookups section of a Flow run card: 'Read the document', then nine rows of 'Searched your folders for' a quoted phrase, each with a 'Retrieved:' filename and a duration between 0.3 and 0.7 seconds."
          caption="Ten lookups · Each one named, timed, and its retrieval stated"
          sizes="(min-width: 900px) 34rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
        />
      </li>
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">The record</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">Recorded cost, and the change pinned to the bytes.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">
            The estimate was 0.000924 USD before the run. The recorded cost after it was
            0.026684 USD, priced from the cost table, with the model and provider named.
            Those are two facts, and Flow keeps them apart. Under them, the saved change is
            pinned to the exact saved document by its before and after digests: Receipt valid.
          </p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail
          src={detailSaved}
          class="w-full max-w-[37.5rem]"
          alt="The Cost and Saved change sections of a Flow run card: 'Recorded cost 0.026684 USD, priced from the cost table', model claude-haiku-4-5, provider anthropic, ran on Cloud, then 'Before the change' and 'After the change' digests and 'Receipt valid'."
          caption="Recorded cost 0.026684 USD · Before and after digests · Receipt valid"
          sizes="(min-width: 900px) 34rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
          glow
        />
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
